/-!
# Cubic closure and placement for the alternating star rows

For the actual component selected from the escaping I, the literal core-to-star
map induces an isomorphism on central quotients. Thus an A₆ or A₇ star row,
or the central quotient of the 3.A₆ row, identifies the central quotient of
X/O₂(X), while retaining its possible central kernel.

The source bound on this center and the three-rank bound in I give relative
normality and identify X with the subgroup generated by the elements of order
three in I. The original wreath quotient similarly shows that K = O²(H) is
generated by its elements of order three. Consequently K lies in C_X(ZS).
The actual S₃ × S₃ quotient of KS then forces three-rank two in both C_X(ZS)
and M₀ = (Mc ∩ I) ∩ X. The genuine earlier Kc premise also rules out X ≤ Mc.

These are placement results for the original component and original K. The
remaining marked-parabolic exclusions and placement of the entire KS are
separate obligations in the assembly of 15.2.23.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 15.2.23, printed pp.1116--1117, A.3.18 and C.2.7;
refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/

